		"PIANO / PROGRAM: Piano level, Program display, Program dial, Shift",
		"SYNTH / EFFECTS: Synth level, Cutoff / FM amount, Resonance / partials, Attack, Release, Delay mix, Reverb mix, Rotary speed"
	],
	"notice": "The 73 and HP versions have a pitch stick and modulation wheel; the 61-key version does not. Use the model-specific manual for MIDI settings and Aux KB routing. Many parameters use NRPN sequences, which are omitted. Match the instrument MIDI channel and receive filters before sending notes or CCs. USB carries MIDI/data rather than audio; connect the audio outputs separately. Consult the download page for the correct Windows USB driver. Port aliases have not been verified on hardware; select the profile manually. The drawings are selected-control schematics rather than scale panel plans. Keyboard and panel controls remain unbound; splits, octave shifts and layer routing can change their behavior. Only the listed CCs are supplied, not the full MIDI implementation.",
